    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. The API is built with Express 5.3.0 and Knex + pg (migrations via Knex CLI, connection string read from `DATABASE_URL` only).\n\n**Files:** `src/app.js` (routes/validation), `src/db.js`, `src/server.js`, `knexfile.js`, `migrations/20261122000000_create_links.js`, `start.sh`, `README.md`\n\n**Verified against the requirements with a live curl battery:**\n- `POST /links` → 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the submitted URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged (no trailing-slash rewriting); auto-generated codes use an 8-char alphabet-safe generator with collision retry\n- Duplicate custom code → 409, unknown codes → 404, all with JSON `error` fields\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with exact stored URL as `Location`, clicks incremented atomically exactly once per request (`UPDATE ... clicks+1 RETURNING`)\n- `GET /links` → `{\"items\", \"total\"}` in ascending creation order; `GET /links/{code}` → full record\n- 422 for malformed JSON (mapped from body-parser's 400), missing/invalid url (relative, ftp, no-host, non-string), and invalid codes (length 3/21, bad chars, non-string)\n- Persistence: restarted the server via `start.sh` — links and click counts (4) survived; `migrate:latest` is idempotent (\"Already up to date\")\n- Edge guard: URLs with non-header-safe characters are rejected as invalid to avoid 500s on the `Location` header\n\nLeft the environment clean: database truncated to 0 links, server stopped, port 8000 free, and `sh start.sh` cold-starts from empty state correctly (confirmed `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0}`)."
